      <!-- Example row of columns -->
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-4">
          <h2>Make Therapy More Effective</h2>
          <p>Less than 1% of waking time is spent in therapy even when meeting on a weekly basis. Growth and change are highly dependent on changing habits and changing habits is dependent on repetition of new responses.</p>
          <p>In/Between Therapy helps you make the most of your therapy by reminding you of important concepts and skills you've discussed with your therapist. That way, you spend more time practicing between therapy sessions so you can reach your goals faster.</p>
          <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#" role="button">View details &raquo;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-4">
          <h2>Increase Collaboration</h2>
          <p>A lot can come up in a therapy session. Sometimes it can be difficult to remember everything that sounded important. Your therapist probably won't know what really stuck for you and what didn't. Consequently, you might not always be on the same page. </p>
          <p>In/Between Therapy helps you and your therapsit to see what is helping between sessions and what isn't, so that you can make targeted adjustments that work best for you.</p>
          <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#" role="button">View details &raquo;</a></p>
       </div>
        <div class="col-lg-4">
          <h2>Have Fun</h2>
          <p>Accomplishing a task feels good. Seeing the positive impact on your goals over time feels better and motivates further progress. </p>
          <p>In/Between Therapy helps you track your growth and shows you what steps to take in order to keep it going.</p>
          <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#" role="button">View details &raquo;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>



